This folder holds Atkinson Hyperlegible Next, version 2.001, as OpenType
(CFF) fonts.

Atkinson Hyperlegible Next is a sans from the Braille Institute, drawn by
Applied Design Works and Letters from Sweden for readers with low vision.
Letters that are easily mistaken for one another, such as I, l and 1 or
O and 0, are given distinct shapes. It covers Latin only, with no Greek
alphabet or Cyrillic.

The family has seven weights, ExtraLight, Light, Regular, Medium,
SemiBold, Bold and ExtraBold, each with an italic, and all fourteen
styles are included here. Regular, Bold and their
italics share the family name Atkinson Hyperlegible Next; the other
weights are found by names such as Atkinson Hyperlegible Next Medium.

The fonts were obtained from

https://github.com/googlefonts/atkinson-hyperlegible-next

(folder fonts/otf) and are licensed under the SIL Open Font License,
version 1.1. The licence text is in OFL.txt.

The atkinson package on CTAN provides LaTeX support for it, through
\usepackage{atkinson}. That package bundles the Braille Institute's own
build of the fonts, with the same family name as the files here. With
LuaLaTeX or XeLaTeX it can also be loaded through fontspec by its family
name, Atkinson Hyperlegible Next.
